---
description: Data, validation, auth, and money/odds rules
globs: src/lib/**/*.ts,src/app/**/route.ts,src/app/**/*.action.ts,prisma/**/*.prisma
---

- **Prisma access is server-only** via the `@/lib/prisma` singleton. Mutations go through
  Server Actions (`*.action.ts`); third-party callbacks/webhooks go through Route Handlers.
- **Validate everything with Zod.** One schema per input (`*.schema.ts`), reused on the
  client (react-hook-form) and re-checked on the server before any write. Never trust the client.
- **Auth + roles enforced server-side** on every gated action/route — never rely on hidden UI.
  Gated capper actions also require a verified email. Hash passwords with `bcryptjs`.
- **Money & odds:** American odds are integers (`-110`, `+150`); units/stakes are
  `Decimal(10,2)`. All payout / profit-loss math lives in `src/lib/grading` — never inline it.
  Grading writes an append-only `GradingAudit` row (source: AUTO / ADMIN_OVERRIDE / MANUAL).
- **Schema isolation:** SCL tables live in the `scl` schema only. Migrations must never touch
  `public`. After any migration, confirm `public` table count is unchanged.
- New env vars: read via `process.env`, document in `.env.example` with a placeholder, never
  commit real values.
